{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1491113-talisman-dedication-vs-talisman-adaptation","id":1491113,"title":"Talisman Dedication vs Talisman Adaptation","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-08-23T12:53:06-07:00","id":1491113,"title":"Talisman Dedication vs Talisman Adaptation","content":"<span style=\"font-size:14px\">Hi guys,<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:arial\">Now that W20 has came out, page 211, it claims that Talisman Dedicated objects can generally resize themselves to accommodate the character's various forms. </span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:arial\">In the Children of Gaia revised, Level 3 Rite, Talisman Adaptation says: <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\">This is similar to the Rite of Talisman Dedication but more powerful. Talismans under this rite actually shapeshift into forms which are usable by the Garou, instead of &quot;disappearing.&quot; Each counts for triple the Gnosis of a dedicated item: A Garou with a 7 Gnosis can have only two items adapted to the new body shape; a Garou might have a vest for tools in her Homid form, which would change into a Crinos-sized vest, and then shapeshift to Lupus, when it would become fitted to the wolf-body. a backpack would become a dog-pack, and so on. Note that frivolous items, such as high heels, stereos, or coffee mugs won't work and will cause loss of 3 permanent Gnosis if adapted.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">So, has W20 Talisman Dedication essentially wiped out Adaptation at this point, or is there a clear difference between the two still? <br /> <br /> If that's the case, it feels like they really buffed Dedication now. Does this mean weapons such as rifles or blades will shape shift into crinos sized weapons? A player asked me this and I just want to give a good answer. I feel like a doofus now since I figured Dedication remained the same across the revisions and never checked W20 until now. It was such a generic, straight forward rite.</span></span></span><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23998-dynamiterave","name":"DynamiteRave","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"16"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-23T13:38:40-07:00","id":1491120,"title":"","content":"Tribebook CoG revised is often regarded as one of the worst books, and Ethan Skemp once admitted in the old White Wolf forum that it was rushed into production without a proper editorial process due to deadlines.<br /> <br /> That said, in my opinion it comes down to the mood of the game you are playing. Do you want a machete to become a razor sharp chunk of metal when the wielder shifts into crinos? Or is that manga territory, suitable for Exalted?<br /> <br /> You could read the W20 Dedication as cloths and back pack straps enlarging, and I would allow that, but in most cases, the player would want them gone in Crinos, for they would be ripped apart in any fight (which is why people shift into crinos). But of course the Klaive's sheath should be present and resize to meet the requirements of each form.<br /> <br /> There was the sentence, that items that belong together should be considered as one item for the purpose of Talisman Dedication, but players should not abuse this rule. In my opinion the same goes for the resize part. It is meant to give the ST and players some freedom, allowing that they have narrative control in some degree. It is not meant to turn a .45 calibre revolver into a anti-vehicle gun by shifting crinos (would the bullet resize itself back to .45 calibre once it left the barrel?).<br /> <br /> So, in my opinion the Talisman Dedication was not buffed, it was given some degree of practicability that frankly I always believed it had - even back in 2nd Edition, simply because it made sense to me. Also, isn't there a garou with an eyepatch in the artwork. Is it a different eyepatch for each form or does it resize? What makes more sense?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1008,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","user":"heinrich","date":". 08-23-2022, 04:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-23T15:19:57-07:00","id":1491129,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>heinrich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1491113-talisman-dedication-vs-talisman-adaptation?p=1491120#post1491120\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Tribebook CoG revised is often regarded as one of the worst books, and Ethan Skemp once admitted in the old White Wolf forum that it was rushed into production without a proper editorial process due to deadlines.<br /> <br /> That said, in my opinion it comes down to the mood of the game you are playing. Do you want a machete to become a razor sharp chunk of metal when the wielder shifts into crinos? Or is that manga territory, suitable for Exalted?<br /> <br /> You could read the W20 Dedication as cloths and back pack straps enlarging, and I would allow that, but in most cases, the player would want them gone in Crinos, for they would be ripped apart in any fight (which is why people shift into crinos). But of course the Klaive's sheath should be present and resize to meet the requirements of each form.<br /> <br /> There was the sentence, that items that belong together should be considered as one item for the purpose of Talisman Dedication, but players should not abuse this rule. In my opinion the same goes for the resize part. It is meant to give the ST and players some freedom, allowing that they have narrative control in some degree. It is not meant to turn a .45 calibre revolver into a anti-vehicle gun by shifting crinos (would the bullet resize itself back to .45 calibre once it left the barrel?).<br /> <br /> So, in my opinion the Talisman Dedication was not buffed, it was given some degree of practicability that frankly I always believed it had - even back in 2nd Edition, simply because it made sense to me. Also, isn't there a garou with an eyepatch in the artwork. Is it a different eyepatch for each form or does it resize? What makes more sense?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I hear you on that. I know that the Coggie book I believe was written by Interns and Ethan even apologized for it. Haha. I don't care for the tribebook at all, but someone was asking about the two rites since I had it listed on a character sheet for an NPC. You made some good points and it was kind of the way I was leaning also. I wasn't going to let a level 1 rite turn a shotgun into an anti-aircraft weapon or what not. I think for the most part, people was wanting to know: Can I wear clothes in crinos?<br /> <br /> I guess the answer is .... sure ... if you want ... LOL","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23998-dynamiterave","name":"DynamiteRave","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"16"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-23T17:08:34-07:00","id":1491147,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DynamiteRave</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1491113-talisman-dedication-vs-talisman-adaptation?p=1491129#post1491129\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I hear you on that. I know that the Coggie book I believe was written by Interns and Ethan even apologized for it. Haha. I don't care for the tribebook at all, but someone was asking about the two rites since I had it listed on a character sheet for an NPC. You made some good points and it was kind of the way I was leaning also. I wasn't going to let a level 1 rite turn a shotgun into an anti-aircraft weapon or what not.</div> </div> </div> </div>Quite right.<br /> <br /> That's a <i>level 5</i> rite.<br /> <br /> (Flaming Death Spears, from Apocalypse)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I think for the most part, people was wanting to know: Can I wear clothes in crinos?<br /> <br /> I guess the answer is .... sure ... if you want ... LOL </div> </div> </div>Well, the new edition is getting rid of the breeding problems, so in a bit of hilarious irony, the rite of clouds and rain can finally come in from the cold! Now, what did it do again?<br /> <br /> Oh, right. I guess it'll need actual mechanics to go along with... anything.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-23T19:38:34-07:00","id":1491152,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1491113-talisman-dedication-vs-talisman-adaptation?p=1491147#post1491147\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, the new edition is getting rid of the breeding problems, so in a bit of hilarious irony, the rite of clouds and rain can finally come in from the cold! Now, what did it do again?<br /> <br /> Oh, right. I guess it'll need actual mechanics to go along with... anything.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was talking to Justin about that and when he said that Metis was no longer a thing, I asked him point blank: So does this mean you're changing the litany and that removes the first tenant? What happens with kinfolk? <br /> <br /> He said it's all on the drawing floor and we'll find out later. <br /> <br /> I feel like this is going to create a lot of garou on garou snuggle times now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23998-dynamiterave","name":"DynamiteRave","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"16"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-23T21:31:46-07:00","id":1491157,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DynamiteRave</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1491113-talisman-dedication-vs-talisman-adaptation?p=1491152#post1491152\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I was talking to Justin about that and when he said that Metis was no longer a thing, I asked him point blank: So does this mean you're changing the litany and that removes the first tenant? What happens with kinfolk?<br /> <br /> He said it's all on the drawing floor and we'll find out later.<br /> <br /> I feel like this is going to create a lot of garou on garou snuggle times now.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, yes. Though, it's also possible that a relationship could be forbidden by politics instead of sacred laws, so that's the reason you don't end up with another Garou.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-23T23:19:37-07:00","id":1491161,"title":"","content":"I wonder if it will be a metaplot advance or a retcon. Meaning, have there never been Crinos-born or is there some change in the workings of the world leading to garou and garou never having kids (or them being homid-born).<br /> A retcon would make compatibility with all that was before a bit more complicated. Older stories like the Tribe Novel series would have characters that should never have been a thing...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-24T01:44:13-07:00","id":1491170,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DynamiteRave</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1491113-talisman-dedication-vs-talisman-adaptation?p=1491129#post1491129\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I guess the answer is .... sure ... if you want ... LOL</div> </div> </div> </div>Welcome to the World of Darkness games, hope you'll like your stay!<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-24T16:34:31-07:00","id":1491258,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>heinrich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1491113-talisman-dedication-vs-talisman-adaptation?p=1491161#post1491161\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wonder if it will be a metaplot advance or a retcon. Meaning, have there never been Crinos-born or is there some change in the workings of the world leading to garou and garou never having kids (or them being homid-born).<br /> A retcon would make compatibility with all that was before a bit more complicated. Older stories like the Tribe Novel series would have characters that should never have been a thing...</div> </div> </div> </div>Technically, one series (Predator and Prey) ignored one rather important part of Crinos-born. And also the whole &quot;Imbued can't have children with monsters&quot; thing, but also the thing about Crinos-born being infertile. Maybe they thought that they were multiplying negatives to get a positive?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-24T18:37:27-07:00","id":1491262,"title":"","content":"There are two things to consider here when deciding if something changes with Dedication or not:<br /> <br /> 1- Would that really change statistics? A big gun isn't necessarily a more efficient gun. From the bullet resizing back in midair to the complex mechanics of the actual shot (which is not just how big my gun is), there may be loads of reasons for it to have the exact same effect. As a rule of thumb, if there's no change in mechanics, there's no need to forbid the character from looking badass. Keep on mind the mood, but otherwise don't worry too much;<br /> <br /> 2- Size change isn't the same as Form change. Dedication changes size for the purpose of safeguarding the item against the effects of the Change, not necessarily to guarantee proper usability, and a Crinos' anatomy is <b><i>extremely</i></b> distinct from a human's. That may very well mean that some objects are harder to use in Crinos, maybe exceedingly so. Klaives are literally <b>made</b> to be used as-is by a Crinos, but any other object you're free to establish higher difficulties and even extra rolls to properly handle in Crinos.<br /> <br /> Of course, both things have fringe cases to be wary of. It's possible that some combinations of Form + Tool will be more effective even if the tool retains the same mechanics, and making up shit for resized objects with the same original form isn't an explored science yet, it may result in some bad calls. But keeping common sense as a general guide should be enough to not go into such traps more than once in a blue moon.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-25T08:02:37-07:00","id":1491302,"title":"","content":"I would not change the statistics of guns.<br /> That said, what are we talking about anyway? Is the actual size of atoms increasing, so the mass would stay the same and therefore the weight and the amount of gunpowder would still match the projectile, given that the gunpowder would react completely with itself, but not need the much smaller oxygen atoms of the surroundings? Remember the &quot;Tiny Ship&quot; episode of DS9 where the needed to beam shrunken oxygen into the compartment they wanted to beam in to breath there? A(u)nt-Man doesn't have that problem...<br /> <br /> Or is the mass increasing to fit the new dimensions? Does the gun become heavier? In that case is the barrel wall width still strong enough to hold the blast of the now increased amount of gunpowder? The required width might not be proportional to the size increase therefore the gun might explode if fired. Also, internal and external ballistics of the gun might change drastically.<br /> <br /> If you try to apply science or engineering thoughts to magical effects you always end up with questions like this. Easiest approach in my opinion is to not read to much into it...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-25T13:57:12-07:00","id":1491342,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>heinrich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1491113-talisman-dedication-vs-talisman-adaptation?p=1491302#post1491302\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would not change the statistics of guns.<br /> That said, what are we talking about anyway? Is the actual size of atoms increasing, so the mass would stay the same and therefore the weight and the amount of gunpowder would still match the projectile, given that the gunpowder would react completely with itself, but not need the much smaller oxygen atoms of the surroundings? Remember the &amp;quot;Tiny Ship&amp;quot; episode of DS9 where the needed to beam shrunken oxygen into the compartment they wanted to beam in to breath there? A(u)nt-Man doesn't have that problem...<br /> <br /> Or is the mass increasing to fit the new dimensions? Does the gun become heavier? In that case is the barrel wall width still strong enough to hold the blast of the now increased amount of gunpowder? The required width might not be proportional to the size increase therefore the gun might explode if fired. Also, internal and external ballistics of the gun might change drastically.<br /> <br /> If you try to apply science or engineering thoughts to magical effects you always end up with questions like this. Easiest approach in my opinion is to not read to much into it...</div> </div> </div> </div>It's... Magic.<br /> <br /> (AKA dont bring rl science into a spirit induced transformation).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","name":"Kakost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-25T14:16:14-07:00","id":1491346,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kakost</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1491113-talisman-dedication-vs-talisman-adaptation?p=1491342#post1491342\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's... Magic.<br /> <br /> (AKA dont bring rl science into a spirit induced transformation).</div> </div> </div> </div>That's what I said.<br /> <br /> But, in all fairness, if one opens the can of wurms and raises questions about game stat changes for weapons not mentioned in the description of the Rite, someone else is allowed to raise questions about other aspects of the Rite, too...<br /> <br /> That is why I prefer Dreamspeaker paradigm, no matter the effect, it's always &quot;spirits did it&quot; and no further explanation needed. People who try to base their magicks in real-world scientific understanding of high-school level physics often do not consider all aspects of the subject at hand.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-25T16:01:06-07:00","id":1491359,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>heinrich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1491113-talisman-dedication-vs-talisman-adaptation?p=1491346#post1491346\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's what I said.<br /> <br /> But, in all fairness, if one opens the can of wurms and raises questions about game stat changes for weapons not mentioned in the description of the Rite, someone else is allowed to raise questions about other aspects of the Rite, too...<br /> <br /> That is why I prefer Dreamspeaker paradigm, no matter the effect, it's always &amp;quot;spirits did it&amp;quot; and no further explanation needed. People who try to base their magicks in real-world scientific understanding of high-school level physics often do not consider all aspects of the subject at hand.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, I was agreeing with you. I dont think that a magic supernatural superpower should be subjected to strict real life scientific scrutiny. If anybody asks how it works, the answer is simple: it's magic!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","name":"Kakost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-25T18:29:59-07:00","id":1491384,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>heinrich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1491113-talisman-dedication-vs-talisman-adaptation?p=1491302#post1491302\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you try to apply science or engineering thoughts to magical effects you always end up with questions like this. Easiest approach in my opinion is to not read to much into it...</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree completely. You can change mechanics if you <b>want</b>, for dramatic effect, but actually nothing you come up will be more realistic than things just working by their normal stats, because the only reasonable conclusions are either that magic keep things equal/changes cancel themselves (like in the atoms growing in size), or physics give up and gun go boom.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}